    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the project's only test class). \n\nDone. I implemented the duplicate-telephone rejection while keeping structural impact minimal \u2014 no existing method was modified, so the per-function cost sum stays low.\n\n**What I added** (behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing an existing class):\n\n1. `EnsureUniqueTelephone.java` \u2014 a new one-method step that reads the built `Owner` (whose telephone was already normalized by `BuildOwner`) and throws if another owner already holds that number. WMC_other = 0.\n2. `DuplicateTelephoneException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (409 mapping).\n3. `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler`.\n4. Escalation YAML wiring the exception to its handler.\n5. Inserted `ensureUnique` between `build` and `save` in `owners.POST.yml`.\n\nThe check sits after normalization so it compares normalized-to-normalized, and before `save` so a conflict is a clean 409 rather than a persisted duplicate. Both new acceptance tests (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`, `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`) and the rest of the suite pass.",
